    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "State the transformation applied to\n$$y=x^2(x-2)^2$$\nto give $y=-x^2(x+2)^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Rotation through $180^\\circ$ about the origin.",
      "worked": "Replace both $x$ and $y$ by their negatives:\n$$\\begin{align*}-y&=(-x)^2(-x-2)^2\\\\-y&=x^2(x+2)^2\\\\y&=-x^2(x+2)^2\\end{align*}$$\nThe two reflections are equivalent to a rotation through $180^\\circ$ about the origin.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
